ROOT CAUSE (tester's analysis, sources read)
  - test-5700.2002.py configure(): no boot system / no boot system backup / get_all_misc /
    createFlashBootImages(self, dut, filenames=[MAIN_RELEASE, BACKUP_RELEASE]) (library_5700.py) ->
    framework ATTools.download_file_from_tftp(self, dut, localFileName=...) with remoteFileName=None ->
    "if remoteFileName is None: remoteFileName = swi.software" = the release the unit is RUNNING.
  - Run 1 (bootloader default restored to 2 -> 9 at triage, Test Engineer 14:05): every 2001 boot was
    "Loading flash:"; 2001 ended on backuprelease.rel ("Switch Current Software: backuprelease.rel"), a name
    tb470 does not serve.
  - Feb control: every 2001 boot was "Loading tftp://10.37.101.1/x230v2-tb101.rel via switchport 2..." with
    "Warning: System has been forced to boot from a non-standard location" (3/3 in swi_a_2001.log; 28 TFTP
    loads + 41 banners in 2002), so swi.software stayed x230v2-tb101.rel -- a served file -- and the same copy
    succeeded ("copy tftp://10.37.101.1/x230v2-tb101.rel flash:/mainrelease.rel").
  => The pristine suite requires the bootloader DEFAULT boot source to be TFTP (the forced-banner state). The
     suite's own recovery() does exactly that (Boot Menu 2 -> 3) but is never called. Not a 6.2.40 result.

